<title>PHILIPPINES: ADB grants funds for Vietnam-Laos-Thailand highway.</title>
<headline>ADB grants funds for Vietnam-Laos-Thailand highway.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank (ADB) on Monday approved a $3.0 million technical assistance grant to improve a highway linking northern Thailand, Laos and Vietnam.</p>
<p>The ADB said in a statement the assistance will fund project preparation activities such as engineering design, civil works procurement and environmental evaluation to improve the 293-km (180-mile) -long highway.</p>
<p>It said the project is part of the ADB's Greater Mekong Subregion initiative to promote peace and prosperity in a region formerly divided by decades of conflict.</p>
<p>The highway links agriculturally rich regions in the three countries to the town of Mukdahan in Thailand and the port city of Da Nang in Vietnam. Traffic density on the highway is expected to reach 700 vehicles per day by the turn of the century from the current 300 vehicles, the ADB said.</p>
</text>
